{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And the might</b> — And these generations will tell the awesome deeds that You did before their eyes, like the signs of Egypt and other awesome wonders. But as for Your greatness — which is the greatness of Your glory — I will tell them; perhaps they will understand." "<b>Now the meaning of Your awesome deeds</b> — for thus it is fitting that the King be awesome."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:47.270602895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}